{
  "window_id": "w0022",
  "observed_failures": [
    "074.jpg total_amount predicted '702.00' instead of correct '102.00' — OCR misread leading '1' as '7' on 'Total Amt Rounded' line; agent's priority tier selected last candidate within tier instead of using cross-line consensus (subtotal=102.00, payment=102.00, total incl GST=102.00 all agree)",
    "077.jpg amount wrong — agent discussion shows 'Total (Excluding GST)' line was being picked before adding Excluding exclusion; general risk that pre-tax 'Excluding'/'Excl.' totals outrank the final inclusive total",
    "078.jpg amount null (delivery shows empty string) — Thai Delicious receipt uses 'Grand Total' label which should match tier 1; likely failed because format uses non-standard spacing or value column alignment",
    "034.jpg date wrong — likely DD/MM vs MM/DD ambiguity or OCR digit confusion not reconciled",
    "071.jpg date risk from OCR misreading '0' as '6' producing invalid month 62; no digit-correction fallback",
    "General: agent spent many iterations hand-tuning per-receipt exclusions and candidate ordering, hit max_iterations=65 without converging"
  ],
  "root_causes": [
    "image-ocr skill lacks a concrete, prioritized total-extraction algorithm: original skill only teaches raw OCR and multi-pass combination but gives no rules for keyword priority tiers, exclusion keywords, two-line fallback, or number normalization that the task prompt explicitly requires",
    "No guidance on cross-candidate consensus (e.g., when multiple total-like lines yield different numbers, prefer the value that also appears in subtotal/payment/change-complement) to defend against single-line OCR digit errors",
    "No guidance on handling impossible dates (month>12, day>31) via digit-confusion correction (0↔6, 1↔7, 8↔3) or by swapping day/month",
    "xlsx skill does not warn that numeric fields intended as fixed-decimal strings (e.g. '47.70') must be written with object dtype / explicit string formatting; risk of pandas coercing to float and losing trailing zero",
    "No skill documents an end-to-end receipt-to-xlsx pipeline template with: directory iteration, per-image try/except → null, filename-sorted output, single-sheet 'results' schema, header row, and no-extra-columns guarantee",
    "image-ocr skill does not recommend upscaling small images or variant preprocessing specifically tuned for faint thermal receipts; agent had to discover this ad hoc",
    "No budget-awareness guidance: skills do not instruct the agent to lock in a working extraction pipeline early and avoid iterative per-image tuning that burns iterations"
  ],
  "skill_defects": [
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "Missing structured-field extraction section for receipts (totals, dates). The 'When to Use' bullet mentions receipts/forms but no code or rules are provided.",
      "evidence": "Original image-ocr skill contains only raw text extraction and multi-pass OCR; task prompt gives explicit keyword priority list and exclusion list that the skill does not encode."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "No normalization rules for monetary values (strip currency prefix like 'RM'/'$', strip comma thousands separators, format to exactly two decimals as string, null-on-failure semantics)."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "No date-parsing/reformatting guidance (ISO YYYY-MM-DD output, handling of DD/MM/YYYY vs MM/DD/YYYY, month-name formats, rejection of impossible dates, optional digit-confusion repair)."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "Multi-pass OCR section aggregates text but does not instruct how to use multiple passes for voting/consensus on structured fields, which is what defends against single-digit OCR errors like 1→7."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "No two-line fallback pattern (keyword on one line, number on the next) despite the task prompt explicitly calling it out."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "No preprocessing recommendation specifically for small/faded receipts (upscale 2x before OCR); agent discovered this manually mid-run."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "defect": "No guidance for writing fixed-decimal string columns (e.g., currency as 'NN.NN' string). Users easily end up with floats and lose trailing zeros / '47.7' vs '47.70' mismatches."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "defect": "No pattern for 'write a dataframe to a single named sheet with exact columns, no index, no extra sheets' — a very common evaluation shape."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "defect": "No guidance on representing null cells cleanly (Python None vs empty string vs NaN) when writing with pandas/openpyxl, which affects exact-match verifiers."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "No end-to-end batch pipeline template (iterate directory, filter by image extension, sort by filename, graceful per-file failure to null row, assemble dataframe)."
    }
  ],
  "repair_recommendations": [
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add a 'Structured Field Extraction from Receipts' section with: (a) exclusion keyword list checked FIRST, (b) priority-ordered keyword tiers (GRAND TOTAL > TOTAL RM/TOTAL: RM > TOTAL AMOUNT > TOTAL/AMOUNT/NET(T) TOTAL/TOTAL DUE/AMOUNT DUE/BALANCE DUE), (c) two-line fallback (last number on next non-empty line when keyword line has no number), (d) number normalization: strip currency prefix, strip commas, require regex that prefers values with two decimals, format output as f\"{v:.2f}\".",
      "scope": "generalizes to any receipt/invoice OCR-to-structured task"
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add a 'Date Extraction' subsection: list of regex+format pairs covering ISO, DD/MM/YYYY, DD-MM-YY, DD Month YYYY; reject dates with month>12 or day>31; optional repair step that tries common digit swaps (6↔0, 1↔7, 8↔3) when a candidate date is otherwise invalid; always emit YYYY-MM-DD or None."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add 'Cross-Pass Consensus' guidance: when multiple OCR passes/preprocessing variants are run, collect all (tier_index, value) candidates and prefer value by (lowest tier_index, highest cross-pass frequency, agreement with subtotal/payment if available). Explicitly document that OCR digit errors are usually isolated to one line, so consensus beats single-line last-match."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add preprocessing recipe for small/faded receipts: convert to grayscale, autocontrast, upscale 2x via LANCZOS when max(dim)<1500, then run PSM 6 as primary with PSM 4 and PSM 11 as fallbacks. Document that this materially helps thermal receipts."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add a 'Batch Pipeline to Tabular Output' section with a reusable function: iterate sorted(os.listdir(dir)) filtered to image extensions, run extract per file inside try/except, record None for failed fields, build a pandas DataFrame with explicit column order, keep string columns as object dtype."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add explicit 'Critical Rules' checklist for receipt extraction: exclusions-first, priority-order-matters, two-line-fallback, strip-currency-and-commas, format-as-two-decimal-string, null-not-NaN-not-'None', sort-by-filename-lexicographically. These rules capture failures observed in this run and generalize to similar tabular OCR tasks."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "change": "Add 'Writing fixed-decimal string columns' subsection: show that currency/amount columns intended to preserve trailing zeros must be stored as Python str via f\"{v:.2f}\" and the column dtype set to object before to_excel; warn against float coercion."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "change": "Add 'Exact-shape single-sheet output' pattern: with pd.ExcelWriter(path, engine='openpyxl') as w: df.to_excel(w, sheet_name='<name>', index=False); emphasize no extra sheets created, header written as row 1, columns in declared order."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "change": "Add 'Null cell semantics' note: for strict verifiers, write Python None (not np.nan, not 'None', not '') for missing values; show how to coerce pandas NaN to None before writing when needed."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "change": "Add a 'Budget discipline' note: once a pipeline passes on 2–3 sample images, run it over the full set once and accept remaining OCR errors as null rather than hand-tuning per-image exclusions; this prevents iteration-limit terminations like the one observed."
    },
    {
      "skill": "openai-vision",
      "change": "Add a brief cross-reference pointing to the new structured-receipt rules in image-ocr so that if openai-vision is used for the same task, the agent still applies the same keyword priority, exclusion, normalization and output-formatting rules."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 0.78
}
